## 🧠 Reflection

Day 17 completely reframed how I view the future of development on the Salesforce platform. Previously, building automation meant writing rigid code paths where every single logical branch had to be hardcoded ahead of time. Agentforce introduces a world where we build modular "tools" (Flows and Apex actions) and let an intelligent reasoning engine determine how to combine them on the fly.

The biggest takeaway from today is that our role as developers is shifting from writing procedural execution flows to becoming **AI Architects**. Success in an AI-driven landscape requires writing exceptionally clean, well-documented, and bulkified platform actions, accompanied by pristine metadata descriptions so the reasoning engine knows exactly when and how to deploy them. Mastering this coordination between programmatic strength and autonomous AI is the defining skill for the next generation of enterprise engineering.
